-- #804/#1028 regression guard.  `Asy` is exported ABSTRACTLY — plain `export`,
-- constructor PRIVATE — which is the standard opacity pattern and exactly how
-- `stdlib/async.mdk` declares `Async (e : Effect) a`.  Its first parameter is
-- Effect-kinded, declared on the head, and that KIND must reach an importer
-- even though the constructor must not: see `registerOpaqueParamKinds` in
-- compiler/types/typecheck.mdk.
--
-- This fixture and test/analyze_project_fixtures/804_opaque_row_iface_accept/ TOGETHER
-- replace the drained must-fail pin 804-abstract-export-row-kind-cross-module: this one
-- takes the SILENT halves (inferred schemes), that one takes the REJECTION half (the pin's
-- located T-EFFECT-UNDETERMINED assertion, inverted to an accept).  Neither covers the
-- other — see the note in entry.mdk.
export data Asy (e : Effect) a = Mk (Unit -> <e> a)
